Next up, we try to evaluate the term using the innermost strategy.

    *OutermostInnermost> evalIM $ fix :@: fac :@: nat 1
    ^CInterrupted.
    
Unfortunately, there are no computations to observe and we enventually need to stop the computation.
When we only compute 50 reduction steps, we can at least take a look at the term so far. The term is pretty hard to parse, however, we can see some repetitions that eventually are a good indicator for the non-terminating computation that is happening here using innermost.

